               <floruit notBefore="1865" notAfter="1910">She was born to a noble family living in
                     <placeName ref="LOC4578Marhab"/>. She was a spouse of King <persName
                     ref="PRS7006Menilek">Mǝnilǝk II</persName> from <date>1865</date> to
                     <date>1882</date>. Although her exact date of birth is unknown, she is believed
                  to be older that the king. <persName ref="PRS7006Menilek">Mǝnilǝk II</persName>
                  and her did not have any children together, but she had five children from
                  previous marriages, three sons and two daughters. At first, she was supportive of
                  her husband’s ambitiones and probably even helped <persName ref="PRS7006Menilek"
                     >Mǝnilǝk II</persName> establish his authority in <placeName
                     ref="LOC4578Marhab"/>. However, spousal conflict escalated in <date>1876</date>
                  when she prevented one of her daughters from marrying <persName
                     ref="PRS6837MasasaS"/>. Later, after participating in the unsuccessful revolt
                  against <persName ref="PRS7006Menilek">Mǝnilǝk II</persName>, she went to
                     <placeName ref="LOC2296DabraL">Dabra Libānos</placeName> and became a
                  nun.</floruit>

               <death when="1900" cert="medium">She died at <placeName ref="LOC2296DabraL">Dabra
                     Libānos</placeName> c. <date>1900</date>.</death>

            </person>
